<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Banjul</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bathurst</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Banjul is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-gambia">The Gambia</a>, on St Mary's Island at the mouth of the Gambia river. It was founded as Bathurst in 1816 by the British, who wanted a base to suppress the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">slave trade</a>, and became the capital of the Gambia colony and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>. It was renamed Banjul in 1973, eight years after independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/banjul.jpg" alt="Banjul" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hannu Sääskilahti · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gambia,_Banjul,_Arch_22.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
